\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Live-campaign results from the persisted artifacts (identical deterministic-strata bars across runs are the finding, not a plotting error). All four plotted values are the \emph  {both-channel} operational score of Table~\ref {tab:live}, which fuses the served-text and CTI-analysis channels; they are not served-quality results, and the echo-guarded bounds for the same rows are 0.479 technique and 0.243 actor. \emph  {Top:} suite means with bootstrap 95\% confidence intervals; open markers mark the independent second run's point estimates, and the actor interval is degenerate ($^{\dagger }$) because the actor rubric assigns the same score to every row, so uncertainty is carried by the Wilson pass-rate interval instead (Table~\ref {tab:live}). \emph  {Bottom:} two independent 218-query campaigns; the deterministic CTI strata replicate exactly and only the LLM-judged persona stratum moves, by $+0.018$.}}{12}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:results}{{3}{12}{Live-campaign results from the persisted artifacts (identical deterministic-strata bars across runs are the finding, not a plotting error). All four plotted values are the \emph {both-channel} operational score of Table~\ref {tab:live}, which fuses the served-text and CTI-analysis channels; they are not served-quality results, and the echo-guarded bounds for the same rows are 0.479 technique and 0.243 actor. \emph {Top:} suite means with bootstrap 95\% confidence intervals; open markers mark the independent second run's point estimates, and the actor interval is degenerate ($^{\dagger }$) because the actor rubric assigns the same score to every row, so uncertainty is carried by the Wilson pass-rate interval instead (Table~\ref {tab:live}). \emph {Bottom:} two independent 218-query campaigns; the deterministic CTI strata replicate exactly and only the LLM-judged persona stratum moves, by $+\RaginPersonaRunDelta $}{figure.3}{}}
