\newlabel{tab:b4}{{2}{13}{Paired RAG-vs-no-RAG differential (180 observations = 90 matched pairs, one per scenario per arm; 95\% bootstrap CIs computed over the 90 per-pair differences). Persona realism is predicted to be retrieval-independent, and is}{table.2}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Paired grounding differential (RAG $-$ No-RAG) per suite with 95\% bootstrap CIs over 90 scenario pairs (numbers in Table~\ref {tab:b4}). Filled markers: intervals excluding zero -- $+0.317$ on technique detection and $+0.140$ on actor attribution. The open marker is the persona stratum, whose interval straddles zero exactly as the architecture predicts: host believability is produced by the deception engine and the fiction graph, not by threat-intelligence retrieval. The mechanism behind the technique effect is starker than the mean: the grounded arm yields 35{} TTP detections spanning 21 distinct techniques, while the ungrounded arm yields none.}}{13}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:grounding}{{4}{13}{Paired grounding differential (RAG $-$ No-RAG) per suite with 95\% bootstrap CIs over 90 scenario pairs (numbers in Table~\ref {tab:b4}). Filled markers: intervals excluding zero -- $+\RaginTechDelta $ on technique detection and $+\RaginActorDelta $ on actor attribution. The open marker is the persona stratum, whose interval straddles zero exactly as the architecture predicts: host believability is produced by the deception engine and the fiction graph, not by threat-intelligence retrieval. The mechanism behind the technique effect is starker than the mean: the grounded arm yields \RaginGroundingTtpCount {} TTP detections spanning 21 distinct techniques, while the ungrounded arm yields none}{figure.4}{}}
